.env.local
node_modules
dist
# The web (Cloudflare Sites) build output. Same content as dist/ but built with
# a root-absolute asset base, and it must never be committed: it contains the
# published APK and every hashed chunk.
dist-web
src/convex/_generated
isolate

# Signing material, wherever it ends up. `android/.gitignore` already covers the
# Android tree, but a keystore or its passwords copied to the repository root —
# the usual accident when someone is in a hurry — must not be committable
# either. The distribution key identifies the app on Play and cannot be
# rotated, so an exposed one is not a mistake that can be undone.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
keystore.properties
keystore.properties.*
!keystore.properties.example
